The PAL's configure on witos (plan step N3.2): LTTng serves the Linux event provider alone, which 8.0
chooses for CLR_CMAKE_HOST_LINUX; witos takes the dummy provider, so the configure does not require LTTng's header, as
10.0 requires it only with FEATURE_EVENTSOURCE_XPLAT.

--- a/src/coreclr/pal/src/configure.cmake
+++ b/src/coreclr/pal/src/configure.cmake
@@ -1272,7 +1272,9 @@
   set(PAL_PT_WRITE_D PT_WRITE_D)
   set(HAS_FTRUNCATE_LENGTH_ISSUE 0)
 else() # Anything else is Linux
-  if(NOT HAVE_LTTNG_TRACEPOINT_H AND FEATURE_EVENT_TRACE)
+  # LTTng serves the Linux event provider alone (eventprovider/CMakeLists.txt); WitOS takes the dummy provider, as 10.0
+  # does for every platform without FEATURE_EVENTSOURCE_XPLAT.
+  if(NOT HAVE_LTTNG_TRACEPOINT_H AND FEATURE_EVENT_TRACE AND NOT CLR_CMAKE_TARGET_WITOS)
     unset(HAVE_LTTNG_TRACEPOINT_H CACHE)
     message(FATAL_ERROR "Cannot find liblttng-ust-dev. Try installing liblttng-ust-dev  (or the appropriate packages for your platform)")
   endif()
